course: dictionary
lesson: 10797
title: Vantage: a good place to see from
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A vantage point is a good place to see from. From a high hill you can see far across a valley, so the hill is a good vantage point. Vantage is a noun, and it is mostly used in the phrase «vantage point».
explain: The word vantage is also short for advantage, which means a good point or a helpful thing. In one story, the Snake shows the Elephant's Trunk, and says: «It can swat flies, pull up grass and slap cool mud on his head, three "'Vantages".» Here each 'vantage is a useful thing the trunk can do.
explain: Check the clues around the word. If the sentence talks about looking, watching or seeing, vantage probably means a good place to view from. If it talks about being better off, it probably means advantage. Then swap your meaning into the sentence to see if it still makes sense.
fact: Vantage is a noun.
fact: A vantage point is a good place to watch or see from.
fact: Vantage can be a short form of advantage, meaning a good point.
fact: Formal writing may use advantage in the same way: «from this vantage» means from this good place or position.
fact: In old UK tennis, vantage was the word used for advantage after deuce.
exercise: «The scout climbed to a vantage point to see the enemy coming.» What is a vantage point? | A fast running race | A deep hole in the ground | *A good place to watch from | A lost bag
exercise: In tennis, what did old UK players call advantage after deuce? | *Vantage | A ball that bounces twice | A tie with no winner | A wooden racket
exercise: Which word is vantage short for? | *advantage | adventure | disadvantage | castle
test: «From this vantage, we could see the whole river.» What does vantage mean here? | A small boat | A kind of bread | A loud noise | *A good place to view from
test: Which is a good vantage point for drawing a landscape? | Inside a shoe box | A deep cave | *A high hill with a wide view | A dark tunnel
exam: Leo says, «From his vantage he could see the whole field.» What is the best meaning? | Standing on a chair | A hidden hole | *A good place to see from, which gives an advantage | A field full of sheep
